import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout pageName="Introduction" currentPath="/">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>
  <p class="doc-intro">
    Semiotic UI is a framework-agnostic Neo-Brutalist UI kit. Its visual language follows Ron Cobb's Semiotic Standard:
    hard borders, zero radius, offset shadows, monospace technical codes and a strict palette of state colors, so an
    interface reads like the control panel of an industrial ship.
  </p>
  <p>
    Components are plain CSS classes with the <span class="sm-code-tag">sm-</span> prefix and native Web Components
    configured only with HTML attributes, so the same markup works in static HTML, server templates and any framework.
  </p>
  <h2>Consumption channels</h2>
  <ul class="doc-channels">
    <li>
      <strong>Applications with a bundler</strong> (Vite, Astro, React): install the package from npm and import the library
      and its stylesheet as ES modules.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Applications with a classic script</strong> (static HTML, Thymeleaf, HTMX): load the compiled stylesheet and
      the UMD script from a CDN or from your own server.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Continue with the <a href="/installation/">Installation</a> guide.</p>
</DocsLayout>
